* 11 Sep 26 dm - THE ONE-SHOT MARKER THAT MAKES ADOPT INSTALL-ONLY, the port's
*   of 21 Aug 2026.  installsdai.sh writes this file immediately before running
*   the verb and removes it again afterwards; more.args accepts ADOPT only
*   while it is there, and deletes it on acceptance.
*
*   ***K$INTERNAL IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN AND THE PORT LEARNED THAT THE HARD
*   WAY.***  Here -internal is behind check_admin() (sd.c:351), so it already
*   means root - but root is exactly who an administrator becomes with sudo,
*   and the owner's rule is that the system AS DELIVERED enforces that SD
*   account setup happens in SD.  A marker makes the door open for one account
*   for one command instead of standing open for anybody who reaches -internal.
*
*   ***IT IS NOT SHIPPED AND MUST NEVER BE.***  A marker in the source tree
*   would be staged into every install and leave the door open permanently,
*   which is the state this replaces.
