*   ASSIGNED HERE rather than in more.args because BCOMP's "is not assigned a
*   value" is what the bootstrap fails on, and more.args is shared by the GROUP
*   and OTHER arms, which never set acc.uname.  The USER arm overwrites it with
*   '$adopt.<name>' as soon as the name is parsed, so one marker authorises one
*   account rather than the verb in general; nothing writes this bare name, so
*   it cannot exist on a delivered system.
   adopt.marker = @sdsys:@ds:'$adopt'
   begin case
   case upcase(acc.type) = 'USER'
*    CREATE.ACCOUNT USER <user acct name>  {NO.QUERY}   
     pathname = CONFIG('USRDIR')
     if pathname = '' then pathname = '/home/sd/user_accounts'
     call @parser(PARSER$GET.TOKEN, token.type, acc.uname, keyword)
