*   !is_user was broken on MSYS2, so repairing the lookup alone would have
*   turned an accidental refusal into a silent adoption.
*
*   MERGED INTO ONE BRANCH, as the port's, because the answer is now the same
*   either way and the downcase only decides which spelling is used.
     case is_user(acc.uname) or is_user(downcase(acc.uname))
       if adopt then
         * The one sanctioned exception, and it is not reachable from a
         * console: ADOPT needs -internal AND a one-shot marker, which means
         * the install path.  No Linux user is created and no password is set -
         * the account is already the person's.
         if is_user(acc.uname) else acc.uname = downcase(acc.uname)
       end else
         @system.return.code = -ER$ARGS
         stop sysmsg(10038, acc.uname) ;* Linux user %1 already exists
       end

* 11 Sep 26 dm - ADOPT NAMED A LINUX USER THAT IS NOT THERE, so there is
*   nothing to adopt.  Creating one instead would be the opposite of what was
*   asked, and it is the branch below that would otherwise do it.
     case adopt
       @system.return.code = -ER$ARGS
       stop sysmsg(6074)  ;*    Invalid user name

     case no.query
* 11 Sep 26 dm - THE REASON WAS WRONG, the port's fix of 14 Aug 2026.  This
*   said "Invalid user name" (6074), but by this point the name is fine - what
*   cannot work is NO.QUERY, because creating a Linux user means setting its
